# sqlx embeds each migration file's exact bytes at compile time and checksums
# them; a file whose working-tree line endings don't match what a fresh
# checkout produces (e.g. one created/edited in place without ever being
# re-checked-out, bypassing core.autocrlf) gets a different checksum on that
# machine than everywhere else, and sqlx refuses to start once any two builds
# disagree. Force CRLF here explicitly so it can't depend on whichever
# core.autocrlf a given clone happens to have.
frontend/src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=crlf
